WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.210
The known part of life is absolutely dull
and boring.

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:09.410
Nobody wants to watch a movie of someone's
life that goes like this: John was born.

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:11.610
He went to school.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:12.960
Then he went to college.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.559
Then he met a girl in college.

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:16.230
Then he got married.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.230
Then they had kids.

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:18.230
Then he had a good job.

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:20.160
The he got fired from his good job.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.369
Then he got a second good job.

00:00:21.369 --> 00:00:23.160
The he got fired from his second good job.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.619
Then he got a third good job.

00:00:24.619 --> 00:00:25.619
Then it was okay.

00:00:25.619 --> 00:00:26.650
They bought a house.

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:29.010
They lived there, the kids met somebody.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.010
They got married.

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:32.279
They became grandparents, they were good grandparents.

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:35.420
They died, 192 people showed up at their funeral.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:36.460
That's it, the end.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.360
No one buys that book.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:39.360
No one buys that book.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.600
Who the hell wants to read that book?

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.250
Except for the people that are related to
him.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:45.870
I think every single one of us wants to have
the story of the person that's born, they

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:51.560
go through a shit load of difficulties, life
is difficult, it's annoying, insecurities,

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:59.120
fear, heavy-duty change, constant challenges,
marital, health, family, finance, all this

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:02.809
type of crap and then all of a sudden they're
going through a bunch of different struggles

00:01:02.809 --> 00:01:06.979
and then they figure it out and then this
idea comes to their mind and things change

00:01:06.979 --> 00:01:11.609
and they start taking it and five other people
decide to join them, and then the enemy comes

00:01:11.609 --> 00:01:15.469
and one of their competitors tries to put
them out of business, and they go against

00:01:15.469 --> 00:01:17.429
the enemy and it becomes a heavy weight fight.

00:01:17.429 --> 00:01:18.950
The become the underdogs.

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:22.729
Nobody expected them to do anything and then
all of a sudden, they win, and they take that

00:01:22.729 --> 00:01:27.850
money and create libraries and take it and
start other businesses, and create 2800 jobs

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:30.390
and make a difference around the world and
BOOM!

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.229
All of a sudden this is what happens.

00:01:32.229 --> 00:01:33.229
People want to know that story.

00:01:33.229 --> 00:01:35.649
And I think everybody wants to live that story.

00:01:35.649 --> 00:01:38.710
And if they didn't want to live that story,
Hollywood would never do good.

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:40.569
Why does Hollywood do good?

00:01:40.569 --> 00:01:44.369
Because for two hours you and I can sit in
a movie theater and for those two hours, we're

00:01:44.369 --> 00:01:45.729
absolutely lost.

00:01:45.729 --> 00:01:51.979
It's as if we're high on drugs, because for
two hours we think we are the Wolf of Wall

00:01:51.979 --> 00:01:53.229
Street.

00:01:53.229 --> 00:01:55.850
We think for two hours we're Braveheart.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:59.259
We think we are the gladiator.

00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:03.209
We think we're Marcus Aurelius.

00:02:03.209 --> 00:02:04.649
We think we're Rocky.

00:02:04.649 --> 00:02:05.649
And then we come out in tears.

00:02:05.649 --> 00:02:08.409
And then we forget about it.

00:02:08.409 --> 00:02:11.401
But a few people come out and say, "I'm not
just going to watch a movie named Rocky.

00:02:11.401 --> 00:02:13.530
I'm going to go be the Rocky in my life.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:14.879
I think that's really want it comes down to.

